s a co-chordal graph. The r-barbell graph is a chordal graph obtained by connecting two copies of a complete graph Kr by a bridge, for example see Figure 1. For r ≥ 3, let G be the complement of the r-barbell graph. Then the independence complex \u0001 of \u0001G is ∆G \u0001= hV\u0001(Kr ), V\u0001(Kr ), {x1 , x2 }i on |V (G)| = 2r. The f -vector of ∆G is 1, 2 r1 , 2 r2 + 1, 2 r3 , 2 r4 , . . . , 2 and dim K[∆G ] = r. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEquidistributions around special kinds of descents and excedances-山东大学新闻网 (https://view.sdu.edu.cn/info/1020/148490.htm)\nciteturn1search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.6 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; In a recent paper ({arXiv:2101.01928v1}) Baril and Kirgizov posed two conjectures on the equidistibution of $(cyc,des_2)\\sim (cyc,pex)$ and $(des,des_2)\\sim (exc,pex)$, where cyc, des and exc are classical statistics counting the numbers of cycles, descents and excedances of permutation, while $des_2$ and $pex$ are numbers of special descents and excedances over permutations. In this paper, using combinatorial theory of J-continued fractions and bijections we confirm and strengthen the second conjecture and expand the first one.\n\n## 学术预告\n\n#### \n\n### Equidistributions around special kinds of descents and excedances\n\n#### \n\nImage发布：山东大学融媒体中心 Image日期：2021年04月06日 点击数：\n\n一、题目\n\nEquidistributions around special kinds of descents and excedances\n\n二、主讲人\n\nPro. Jiang Zeng Université Claude Bernard Lyon\n\n三、摘要\n\nIn a recent paper ({arXiv:2101.01928v1}) Baril and Kirgizov posed two conjectures on the equidistibution of $(cyc,des_2)\\sim (cyc,pex)$ and $(des,des_2)\\sim (exc,pex)$, where cyc, des and exc are classical statistics counting the numbers of cycles, descents and excedances of permutation, while $des_2$ and $pex$ are numbers of special descents and excedances over permutations. In this paper, using combinatorial theory of J-continued fractions and bijections we confirm and strengthen the second conjecture and expand the first one.\n\n四、时间\n\n2021.4.9 15: 30 - 17: 00\n\n五、地点\n\nWemeet ID: 645 379 265\n\n六、主讲人简介\n\n曾江，法国里昂第一大学特级教授，博士师从组合数学国际权威 Dominique Foata教授。他曾是美国普林斯顿高等研究院的访问学者，法国斯特拉斯堡大学maître de conférences和南开大学特聘讲座教授。曾教授是法国组合数学学派的杰出代表，并且是里昂大学组合数学团队的学术带头人。他的工作深刻而广泛，成果卓越，是特殊函数、排列统计量和连分式的组合理论方面的专家。\n\n七、主办单位\n\n数学与交叉科学研究中心\n\n〖供稿单位：数学与交叉科学研究中心     作者：杨媛    责任编辑：卞悦悦 蒋晓涵〗--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe 2-balanced double tree decomposition conjecture | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/354571/the-2-balanced-double-tree-decomposition-conjecture)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # The 2-balanced double tree decomposition conjecture ... The paper proves that every double tree has a decomposition that is $4$4-balanced, improving the previously known bound of five.\n\n# The 2-balanced double tree decomposition conjecture\n\nAbout 4 years old · traced to 2022\n\nA double tree is a graph formed by taking two trees on the same vertex set, with the two edge sets regarded as distinct even when they join the same pair of vertices. A double tree decomposition partitions the edges of a double tree into two trees. Such a decomposition is $k$k-balanced if, at every vertex, the absolute difference between its degrees in the two trees is at most $k$k.\n\n2-balanced double tree decomposition conjecture. Any double tree has a $2$2-balanced double tree decomposition.\n\nThe paper proves that every double tree has a decomposition that is $4$4-balanced, improving the previously known bound of five. Examples are known that admit a $2$2-balanced decomposition but no $1$1-balanced one, so the conjectured bound would be best possible; the conjecture remains open.\n\nReferences\n\n## Primary source\n\nFreddie Illingworth, Emil Powierski, Alex Scott and Youri Tamitegama, “Balancing connected colourings of graphs”, arXiv:2205.04984 (2022).\n\ngraph-colouringsgraph-theorytree-decompositions\n\n0 0\n\nPosted 1 month ago\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh Never refreshed\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n## Solutions 0\n\n[Button: Post a solution]\n\n[Button: Solve with an agent]\n\nNo solutions have been posted yet.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEquidistributions around special kinds of descents and excedances (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/350371837_Equidistributions_around_special_kinds_of_descents_and_excedances)\nciteturn1search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; In a recent paper ({arXiv:2101.01928v1}) Baril and Kirgizov posed two conjectures on the equidistibution of $(cyc, des_2)\\sim (cyc, pex)$ and $(des, des_2)\\sim (exc, pex)$, where cyc, des and exc are classical statistics counting the numbers of cycles, descents and excedances of permutation, while $des_2$ and pex are numbers of special descents and excedances over permutations. In this paper, using combinatorial theory of J-continued fractions and bijections we confirm and strengthen the second conjecture and expand the first one.\n\n# Equidistributions around special kinds of descents and excedances\n\n  * March 2021\n\nDOI:10.48550/arXiv.2103.13092\n\nAuthors:\n\nBin Han\n\n  * University of Gothenburg\n\nJianxi Mao\n\n  * Dalian University of Technology\n\nJiang Zeng\n\n  * Claude Bernard University Lyon 1\n\n## Abstract\n\nIn a recent paper ({arXiv:2101.01928v1}) Baril and Kirgizov posed two conjectures on the equidistibution of $(cyc, des_2)\\sim (cyc, pex)$ and $(des, des_2)\\sim (exc, pex)$, where cyc, des and exc are classical statistics counting the numbers of cycles, descents and excedances of permutation, while $des_2$ and pex are numbers of special descents and excedances over permutations. In this paper, using combinatorial theory of J-continued fractions and bijections we confirm and strengthen the second conjecture and expand the first one.\n\n\n## No file available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the file of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nRequest file PDF\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn the Eliahou and Villarreal conjecture about the... (https://arxivlens.com/paperview/details/on-the-eliahou-and-villarreal-conjecture-about-the-projective-dimension-of-co-chordal-graphs-2100-1706448)\nciteturn1search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.8 years ago; Crawled: 4 weeks ago; Back ArXiv math.AC On the Eliahou and Villarreal conjecture about the projective dimension of co-chordal graphs ... 2205.07059 Published Jan 24, 2023 2 citations\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTransformation à la Foata for special kinds of descents and excedances (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/367824911_Transformation_a_la_Foata_for_special_kinds_of_descents_and_excedances)\nciteturn1search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; In a recent paper [1] Baril and Kirgizov considered some special descents, excedances, and cycles of permutations that we recall in the following. ... In particular, we confirm and strengthen Conjecture 1.2 (see Corollary 1.6) and obtain five equidistributed companions of the bistatistic (pex, cyc) in Conjecture 1.1 (see Theorem 1.7). ...\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTransformation \\`a la Foata for special kinds of descents and excedances (https://www.academia.edu/126776895/Transformation_a_la_Foata_for_special_kinds_of_descents_and_excedances)\nciteturn1search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.6 years ago; Crawled: today; arXiv:2101.01928v2 [math.CO] 17 Mar 2021 Transformation à la Foata for special kinds of descents and excedances Jean-Luc Baril and Sergey Kirgizov LIB, Université Bourgogne Franche-Comté B.P.\n----------------------